  "result": "All four tests pass under the venv's Python 3.12, and `catalog/service.py` is the only new source file. I did not commit anything since that wasn't requested.\n\n**Approach chosen: A, sequential integers.** The spec calls for a single in-memory catalog with no cross-process or client-side id generation, so UUIDs' coordination-free uniqueness buys nothing here, while short sortable ids are easier to read in tests and logs. The counter never rewinds, so a deleted record's id is never reused, which keeps ids stable and unique for the catalog's lifetime as the spec requires.\n\nImplementation notes:\n- Records live in an insertion-ordered dict keyed by id, so listing in creation order is free and deletion keeps the order of the survivors.\n- `get`, `update`, and `list` return copies, so callers can't mutate internal state through the returned dicts.\n- `update` validates field names before touching the record, so a bad field on an existing id raises `ValueError` without a partial write.",
